{
    "//":  "Dependency lock for the autotest framework, derived from the resolved ComTestTool venv (D:/Code/ComTestTool/.venv). Versions are the ones that environment actually runs; every wheel was re-resolved for cp312/win_amd64 because the artifact ships CPython 3.12 while the venv is 3.11.",
    "//where":  "\u003capp dir\u003e/python-extras/framework-deps/site-packages, appended to PYTHONPATH for the bundled interpreter by default (apps/desktop/electron/main/python-runtime.ts, frameworkDepsSitePackages).",
    "//whySeparate":  "This stack pins numpy 2.x with opencv\u003c4.12 so paddlepaddle-era code keeps working, while the bundled Office stack pins numpy 2.5.4 for its own wheels. One site-packages cannot satisfy both, so they are installed separately and both reach the interpreter through PYTHONPATH.",
    "//excluded":  "Dev tooling only (pytest, coverage, mypy, ruff and their transitive helpers), the project itself, and uptime (no cp312 wheel, and no reference anywhere in core/libs/hal/utils). setuptools, wheel and setuptools-cpp stay: pyxcp requires setuptools-cpp at import time.",
    "platform":  "windows-x86_64",
    "python":  "3.12",
    "//scope":  "The framework package itself ships source, its vendor CAN driver distribution and its firmware images. Python libraries live here, not in the package.",
